Here's how to handle each scenario with MSTest:

### 1. Windows-only tests

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[OSCondition(OperatingSystems.Windows)]  // custom attribute, or:
public void RegistryTest()
{
    if (!OperatingSystem.IsWindows())
    {
        Assert.Inconclusive("Requires Windows.");
        return;
    }
    // registry code here
}
```

### 2. Skip in CI (requires local GPU)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GpuTest()
{
    if (Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("CI") == "true")
    {
        Assert.Inconclusive("Skipped in CI — requires local GPU.");
        return;
    }
    // GPU test logic
}
```

Or use a custom condition attribute:

```csharp
[AttributeUsage(AttributeTargets.Method)]
public class SkipInCIAttribute : Attribute, ITestDataSource { /* ... */ }
```

### 3. Flaky external API — retry with `[TestCategory]`

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("Flaky")]
[Retry(3)] // MSTest v3.8+ built-in retry
public void WeatherApiTest()
{
    var result = CallWeatherApi();
    Assert.IsNotNull(result);
}
```

> **`[Retry(n)]`** is available in **MSTest 3.8+**. For older versions, implement retry logic manually or use a custom attribute.

### 4. Cleanup even on failure — use `[TestCleanup]` or `try/finally`

```csharp
[TestClass]
public class TempFileTests
{
    private string _tempFile = null!;

    [TestInitialize]
    public void Setup()
    {
        _tempFile = Path.GetTempFileName();
    }

    [TestCleanup] // Runs after EVERY test, even on failure
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        if (File.Exists(_tempFile))
            File.Delete(_tempFile);
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void ProcessTempFile()
    {
        File.WriteAllText(_tempFile, "data");
        // test logic — if this throws, Cleanup still runs
    }
}
```

For one-off cases, `try/finally` works too:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void InlineCleanup()
{
    var tmp = Path.GetTempFileName();
    try
    {
        File.WriteAllText(tmp, "test");
        Assert.IsTrue(File.Exists(tmp));
    }
    finally
    {
        File.Delete(tmp);
    }
}
```

**Summary:**

| Scenario | Approach |
|---|---|
| OS-specific | `Assert.Inconclusive()` guard or custom attribute |
| Skip in CI | Check `CI` env var, `Assert.Inconclusive()` |
| Flaky test | `[Retry(3)]` (MSTest 3.8+) |
| Guaranteed cleanup | `[TestCleanup]` or `try/finally` |
